<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Protectorate</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A protectorate is a territory that retains its own ruler and some internal autonomy but is placed under the control and protection of a stronger state, usually in foreign affairs and defence. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> used protectorates widely, for example in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-region-nigeria">Northern Nigeria</a> from 1900, which covered much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-oyo">New Oyo</a>, the successor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a>, was also a British protectorate.</p></div>
